<title>FINLAND: FINNISH MAY TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 3 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>FINNISH MAY TIMBER CUTTINGS DOWN 3 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of raw timber cuttings fell three percent year-on-year in May to 2.6 milllion cubic metres, the Finnish Forest Research Institute (METLA) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Logwood timber cuttings fell six percent year-on-year to less than 1.3 million cubic metres -- 11 percent below the average in the month of May in 1987-1996, METLA said.</p>
<p>Pulpwood timber cuttings were flat year-on-year, but a quarter below the average, is said.</p>
<p>The volume of raw timber cuttings in January-May rose 11 percent year-on-year to 20.4 million cubic metres.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +359-9-680 50 248, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
